; ============================================================================
;  RECIP.INC - the divide, minted once: 256 cells, one WORD each, holding
;  d/z in 8.8 fixed point with d = 270 - that is round(270 * 256 / z), read
;  at row z. Multiply a coordinate by a cell through IMUL and shift the
;  product right eight places (/256), and out comes x*d/z in pixels with
;  no DIV anywhere: a lookup, a multiply, a shift - the sine table's three
;  moves, aimed at division.
;
;  THE TABLE HAS NO ROW ZERO. Rows 0..94 hold 0, on purpose. A depth
;  that close has no honest reciprocal - the divide this replaces would
;  overflow its register and fire INT 0 - so a vertex that reads here
;  collapses to the centre of the screen instead of crashing the machine.
;  The NEAR PLANE, at 95, is the program's promise never to ask. Row 255
;  is the FAR plane: a depth past a byte has no address at all.
;
;  GENERATED by TOOLS\RecipTab (dotnet run --project TOOLS\RecipTab -- <path>).
;  Nobody typed these numbers. Every DOS engine that drew a corridor had a
;  table like this one, and none of them typed theirs either.
; ============================================================================
RECIP:
